  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hola Tom, recibimos tu solicitud. Revisamos tu cuenta: los intentos fallidos vienen de la red de la oficina en horario laboral, lo que suele pasar cuando un dispositivo (por ejemplo, la app de correo de tu teléfono) sigue usando una contraseña anterior. Ya enviamos la solicitud para desbloquear tu cuenta y un técnico la aprobará pronto; te avisaremos cuando esté lista. Cuando puedas entrar, actualiza la contraseña guardada en tu teléfono y en cualquier otro dispositivo para que la cuenta no se vuelva a bloquear. Si no recuerdas tu contraseña actual, responde a este correo o llámanos al número de soporte para verificar tu identidad y ayudarte a restablecerla.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user: account status locked, 5 failed_login_count, not disabled, not VIP, sign_in_blocked false, VPN enabled. Sign-in logs (14 days): 5 failed_password attempts all on m365 from corporate IP 203.0.113.10 between 09:20 and 09:32 New York time (within usual hours). Interleaved with a successful duo_push sign-in from the same IP at 09:28, and VPN/M365 successes from the usual corporate and residential IPs over the past two weeks. No hosting networks, no foreign locations, no overnight attempts, no MFA denials. Pattern matches KB-001 (saved old password on a device), not an attack, so KB-031 not triggered. Duo push enrolled on Tom's phone. Requested unlock_account (pending technician approval). Did not request reset_password since user has a working current password and no evidence he forgot it; reset only if he cannot recall it. Tech: after unlock, confirm the account does not re-lock within an hour; if it does, escalate per KB-001. Note the password_last_set date (2026-07-23) predates the failures, so a stale saved credential is plausible but the user should be asked which device is still prompting for a password.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-001"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
